# DTF tier manifest: virtual-member-metadata-timeout
#   (artifact-keeper#4508; fixed in 1.11.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + upstreams=mock-multi (the stdlib-python
# upstream at 172.16.<slot>.91; its /hang/... paths accept a request and never
# answer, i.e. a Remote member whose upstream is down with connections
# blackholed rather than refused).
#
# THE BUG
# #4508  A virtual repository whose Remote member stopped answering held every
#        metadata request that reached that member for the upstream client's
#        60 s read timeout, longer than a reverse proxy allows a request, so
#        clients saw 504 and builds crawled (reported on Maven
#        `maven-metadata.xml`). Fixed: each Remote member's metadata fetch is
#        bounded by AK_VIRTUAL_MEMBER_METADATA_TIMEOUT_SECS (default 20); a
#        member that misses it fails the request promptly with a 502 naming
#        it (Maven merges, Helm/CRAN/Hex/Bazel indexes), or is reported in
#        `X-AK-Partial-Members` when the virtual allows partial merges.
#        Metric: ak_virtual_member_metadata_timeouts_total{member}. Artifact
#        downloads are not bounded by it.
#
# SINCE 1.12.0 (artifact-keeper#5621, PR #5809): a member that is unavailable
#        (upstream 5xx, transport error, past the member deadline) is left out
#        of a Helm / CRAN / Hex / Puppet / Bazel / Maven merge and the
#        healthy merge is served 200 with X-AK-Partial-Members naming it and
#        Cache-Control: no-store, partial opt-in or not; the strict 502 now
#        applies only to a member whose document does not parse. On main the
#        failing-member cases assert that; release/1.11.x keeps the 502.
#
# The deadline is lowered to 8 s so the tier is quick and the knob itself is
# proven (the partial answer is timed against the 8 s bound); the fixed
# image must answer well inside 15 s, the 1.10.0 baseline needs the full
# 60 s and the oracle gives up on it at 40 s.
#
# RED image: ak-backend:1.10.0. GREEN: 1.11.0 and later.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: one admin login and ~20 API calls back to back.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-multi"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
export AK_VIRTUAL_MEMBER_METADATA_TIMEOUT_SECS="8"
